Several recent letters have suggested that a character should
be able to choose his alignment for himself.  I disagree.  If
I could play a wizard as a lawful character, it would be the
only character I'd play.  The special abilities of a magic user
coupled with an ability to create lawful altars would make for
a very good character.  As the game stands I often choose to play
a samuri (or a priest) because of the need for good water.

Also, a note on named weapons:



You can collect all of the weapons you find into a big
pile and polymorph it.  If you have several screenfuls
of useless rubber hoses and knives, you might get a
named weapon after just a few tries.  I once had five
named weapons of various types and five Dragonbane's.


